Python Disk Usage Monitoring

=> Objective

The goal of this mini project is to monitor Linux disk usage using Python.

The script:

Runs the Linux df -h / command.
Captures the command output.
Extracts the disk usage percentage.
Converts the value into an integer.
Compares it with a predefined threshold.
Displays OK or WARNING based on disk usage.

=> Program:

import subprocess

result = subprocess.run(
    ["df", "-h", "/"],
    capture_output=True,
    text=True
)

lines = result.stdout.splitlines()

parts = lines[1].split()

disk_usage = parts[4].replace("%", "")

disk_usage = int(disk_usage)

disk_threshold = 80

print("Disk Usage:", disk_usage, "%")

if disk_usage >= disk_threshold:
    print("WARNING: Disk usage is high")
else:
    print("Disk usage is OK")

=> Run:

python3 disk_threshold.py

You might get:

Disk Usage: 75 %
Disk usage is OK

Or:

Disk Usage: 85 %
WARNING: Disk usage is high

depending on your VM.
